{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For I will not go up in your midst.</b> They shall not make a tabernacle, for I will not dwell in the midst of the children of Israel." "<b>And the meaning of lest I consume you on the way.</b> If they do another time like this deed, I will consume them immediately. And a small pataḥ comes in place of a gadol, and the lamed was not given a dagesh, because the grammatical form is thus, like אֲחַוְך hear me (Job 15:17)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "'And a small pataḥ comes in place of a gadol' refers to the shva/pataḥ under the alef of אכלך (אֲכָלְךָ); Ibn Ezra explains why the lamed lacks a dagesh despite following what would normally be a pataḥ gadol pattern."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:01.133021135Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}